00:37:42.040 --> 00:37:43.939
So we would go up there on like Saturdays or something.

00:37:44.040 --> 00:37:44.939
And she could pray,

00:37:45.040 --> 00:37:46.939
I mean, for hours.

00:37:47.040 --> 00:37:47.939
And I was like,

00:37:48.040 --> 00:37:50.939
I have run out of words.

00:37:51.040 --> 00:37:52.939
I don't know.

00:37:53.040 --> 00:37:54.939
I don't know what else to say.

00:37:55.040 --> 00:37:57.939
And I think that's, yeah,

00:37:58.040 --> 00:37:58.939
so that's kind of how I often thought of prayer.

00:37:59.040 --> 00:37:59.939
It's like, well, that's Matthew 6,

00:38:00.040 --> 00:38:01.939
like just do that.

00:38:02.040 --> 00:38:02.939
And pray with words.

00:38:03.040 --> 00:38:04.939
Then later in my life,

00:38:05.040 --> 00:38:07.939
I learned about more of a Romans 8,

00:38:08.040 --> 00:38:09.939
a wordless prayer,

00:38:10.040 --> 00:38:11.939
sometimes even a groaning prayer.

00:38:12.040 --> 00:38:13.939
Prayer without words.

00:38:14.040 --> 00:38:14.939
Kind of a,

00:38:15.040 --> 00:38:15.939
I think of the Psalms,

00:38:16.040 --> 00:38:17.939
be still and know that I am God.

00:38:18.040 --> 00:38:20.939
Really just a prayer of pure presence.

00:38:20.939 --> 00:38:22.840
Just an awareness of God.

00:38:22.939 --> 00:38:24.840
You're there.

00:38:24.939 --> 00:38:25.840
And I'm here.

00:38:25.939 --> 00:38:28.840
And I'm present to you.

00:38:28.939 --> 00:38:30.840
And when I really got into that,

00:38:30.939 --> 00:38:32.840
I started to look down a little bit

00:38:32.939 --> 00:38:33.840
on the word,

00:38:33.939 --> 00:38:34.840
on the wordy prayers.

00:38:34.939 --> 00:38:35.840
Because, you know, in my mind,

00:38:35.939 --> 00:38:37.840
like to pray with words

00:38:37.939 --> 00:38:39.840
was to be, you know,

00:38:39.939 --> 00:38:41.840
active and busy-minded and,

00:38:41.939 --> 00:38:43.840
you know, so wordy.

00:38:43.939 --> 00:38:44.840
And I was just like, ah, I can't.

00:38:44.939 --> 00:38:45.840
But here's the thing,

00:38:45.939 --> 00:38:47.840
as I've just kept going,

00:38:47.939 --> 00:38:48.840
you know how you go through like seasons in your life,

00:38:48.939 --> 00:38:49.840
you know,

00:38:49.840 --> 00:38:50.739
and like the pendulum swings.

00:38:50.840 --> 00:38:51.739
You're like really into this

00:38:51.840 --> 00:38:52.739
and then you're really into that.

00:38:52.840 --> 00:38:53.739
You know what I mean?

00:38:53.840 --> 00:38:54.739
But through it all,

00:38:54.840 --> 00:38:55.739
you're kind of finding your way.

00:38:55.840 --> 00:38:56.739
And that's kind of my journey.

00:38:56.840 --> 00:38:58.739
Like just finding my way.

00:38:58.840 --> 00:39:00.739
And the longer I've journeyed,

00:39:00.840 --> 00:39:03.739
the more these have kind of converged.

00:39:03.840 --> 00:39:04.739
Where in the end,

00:39:04.840 --> 00:39:09.739
I've realized like to,

00:39:09.840 --> 00:39:11.739
that the end point is the same.

00:39:11.840 --> 00:39:13.739
It really is the quality

00:39:13.840 --> 00:39:16.739
of your presence to God.

00:39:16.840 --> 00:39:18.739
Like that's the main thing.

00:39:18.840 --> 00:39:19.739
I don't think God's like,

00:39:19.840 --> 00:39:21.739
oh, I wish you'd use better words, you know.

00:39:21.840 --> 00:39:24.739
I don't think God's overly concerned with that.

00:39:24.840 --> 00:39:26.739
Ultimately, it's about,

00:39:26.840 --> 00:39:28.739
it's love.

00:39:28.840 --> 00:39:29.739
It's love.

00:39:29.840 --> 00:39:33.739
And I've also found

00:39:33.840 --> 00:39:35.739
that one form of prayer

00:39:35.840 --> 00:39:38.739
tends to lead into the other.

00:39:38.840 --> 00:39:39.739
So, and this is something

00:39:39.840 --> 00:39:41.739
Coakley mentions in her quote.

00:39:41.840 --> 00:39:42.739
Where she describes how,

00:39:42.840 --> 00:39:43.739
like for example,

00:39:43.840 --> 00:39:44.739
praying with words,

00:39:44.840 --> 00:39:45.739
say you pray the Lord's Prayer.

00:39:45.840 --> 00:39:47.739
If you pray that long enough,

00:39:47.840 --> 00:39:48.739
eventually you realize

00:39:48.739 --> 00:39:49.639
what Coakley names,

00:39:49.739 --> 00:39:50.639
that you do not know

00:39:50.739 --> 00:39:52.639
what you are praying.

00:39:52.739 --> 00:39:53.639
Like you think you know.

00:39:53.739 --> 00:39:54.639
You're like, oh,

00:39:54.739 --> 00:39:55.639
I'm praying for the kingdom to come.

00:39:55.739 --> 00:39:57.639
Yeah, what does that mean?

00:39:57.739 --> 00:39:59.639
You know, and that's a big question, right?

00:39:59.739 --> 00:40:00.639
I mean, you have some idea,

00:40:00.739 --> 00:40:02.639
but the further you journey into that,

00:40:02.739 --> 00:40:03.639
you realize, oh,

00:40:03.739 --> 00:40:04.639
I actually have no idea

00:40:04.739 --> 00:40:05.639
what that means.

00:40:05.739 --> 00:40:06.639
Like I think I know,

00:40:06.739 --> 00:40:07.639
but I really don't know.

00:40:07.739 --> 00:40:08.639
Or God, I mean,

00:40:08.739 --> 00:40:09.639
that's quite a prayer, right?

00:40:09.739 --> 00:40:10.639
Lord, your kingdom.

00:40:10.739 --> 00:40:11.639
In other words,

00:40:11.739 --> 00:40:14.639
your reality, God.

00:40:14.739 --> 00:40:16.639
Come here.

00:40:17.639 --> 00:40:19.540
What would that mean?

00:40:19.639 --> 00:40:20.540
What would that change?

00:40:20.639 --> 00:40:21.540
What would that invite me into?

00:40:21.639 --> 00:40:24.540
What would that invite you into?

00:40:24.639 --> 00:40:25.540
Right, can you see where

00:40:25.639 --> 00:40:26.540
it's like, oh,

00:40:26.639 --> 00:40:27.540
that's a big prayer.

00:40:27.639 --> 00:40:28.540
I'm not sure what I'm praying.

00:40:28.639 --> 00:40:33.540
Or God, your will be done.

00:40:33.639 --> 00:40:34.540
I mean, it's easy to say.

00:40:34.639 --> 00:40:35.540
You know, it's like,

00:40:35.639 --> 00:40:36.540
oh, Lord, your kingdom come.

00:40:36.639 --> 00:40:37.540
Your will be done.

00:40:37.639 --> 00:40:38.540
Heaven give us day or day.

00:40:38.639 --> 00:40:39.540
You know, you know.

00:40:39.639 --> 00:40:40.540
Busy before I go to work,

00:40:40.639 --> 00:40:41.540
so I got to hurry.

00:40:41.639 --> 00:40:42.540
It's like those are big.

00:40:42.639 --> 00:40:43.540
That's big.

00:40:43.639 --> 00:40:44.540
So you can see where

00:40:44.639 --> 00:40:45.540
a prayer with words,

00:40:45.540 --> 00:40:46.439
it just might lead you

00:40:46.540 --> 00:40:49.439
to a place of silence.

00:40:49.540 --> 00:40:50.439
Where you might say,

00:40:50.540 --> 00:40:53.439
Lord, your kingdom come.

00:40:53.540 --> 00:40:55.439
And then find yourself

00:40:55.540 --> 00:40:57.439
real quiet for a while.

00:40:57.540 --> 00:40:59.439
And vice versa.

00:40:59.540 --> 00:41:01.439
As you pray without words,

00:41:01.540 --> 00:41:03.439
if you feel drawn to silence,

00:41:03.540 --> 00:41:04.439
you might find that

00:41:04.540 --> 00:41:05.439
from that place,

00:41:05.540 --> 00:41:07.439
suddenly a yearning

00:41:07.540 --> 00:41:09.439
comes over you

00:41:09.540 --> 00:41:11.439
to speak

00:41:11.540 --> 00:41:12.439
on behalf of yourself,

00:41:12.540 --> 00:41:13.439
your community,

00:41:13.540 --> 00:41:14.439
your family,

00:41:14.439 --> 00:41:16.340
people you love,

00:41:16.439 --> 00:41:18.340
the world.

00:41:18.439 --> 00:41:19.340
Right?

00:41:19.439 --> 00:41:20.340
In other words, Romans 8

00:41:20.439 --> 00:41:22.340
can lead you into Matthew 6,

00:41:22.439 --> 00:41:24.340
and Matthew 6 can lead you

00:41:24.439 --> 00:41:26.340
back into Romans 8.

00:41:26.439 --> 00:41:27.340
But whether you're praying

00:41:27.439 --> 00:41:29.340
with or without words,

00:41:29.439 --> 00:41:30.340
that's really neither here

00:41:30.439 --> 00:41:31.340
nor there.

00:41:31.439 --> 00:41:32.340
At the end of the day,

00:41:32.439 --> 00:41:33.340
it's the main thing

00:41:33.439 --> 00:41:34.340
is the quality of our attention

00:41:34.439 --> 00:41:35.340
and our presence.

00:41:35.439 --> 00:41:36.340
Now, I think this might

00:41:36.439 --> 00:41:38.340
naturally bring up the question

00:41:38.439 --> 00:41:39.340
which leads us to

00:41:39.439 --> 00:41:40.340
insight number two.

00:41:40.439 --> 00:41:41.340
You say, what on earth

00:41:41.439 --> 00:41:42.340
do you mean by quality

00:41:42.439 --> 00:41:44.340
of my attention and presence?

00:41:44.439 --> 00:41:45.340
I'm so glad you asked.

00:41:45.439 --> 00:41:47.340
So, part of why

00:41:47.439 --> 00:41:49.340
we struggle at prayer

00:41:49.439 --> 00:41:51.340
is because our default

00:41:51.439 --> 00:41:52.340
mental mode

00:41:52.439 --> 00:41:54.340
is mostly one of stress,

00:41:54.439 --> 00:41:56.340
hurry, worry, and blurry.

00:41:56.439 --> 00:41:57.340
Right?

00:41:57.439 --> 00:41:58.340
In other words,

00:41:58.439 --> 00:41:59.340
the quality of our attention

00:41:59.439 --> 00:42:00.340
and presence

00:42:00.439 --> 00:42:01.340
is quite poor.

00:42:01.439 --> 00:42:02.340
This is why, for example,

00:42:02.439 --> 00:42:04.340
I could, with the woman

00:42:04.439 --> 00:42:05.340
at that church,

00:42:05.439 --> 00:42:06.340
she invited me to pray.

00:42:06.439 --> 00:42:07.340
This is why she just

00:42:07.439 --> 00:42:08.340
adored those times.

00:42:08.439 --> 00:42:09.340
Oh, my goodness.

00:42:09.439 --> 00:42:10.340
Three hours to her

00:42:10.439 --> 00:42:12.340
was nothing.

00:42:12.439 --> 00:42:14.340
And I was like,

00:42:14.439 --> 00:42:15.340
20 minutes in, like,

00:42:15.439 --> 00:42:16.340
oh, my gosh,

00:42:16.439 --> 00:42:17.340
how long are we going

00:42:17.439 --> 00:42:19.340
to be here?

00:42:19.439 --> 00:42:21.340
What was the difference there?

00:42:21.439 --> 00:42:22.340
Well, she had been doing

00:42:22.439 --> 00:42:24.340
that for 20 years.

00:42:24.439 --> 00:42:25.340
And so, the quality

00:42:25.439 --> 00:42:26.340
of her attention

00:42:26.439 --> 00:42:27.340
and her presence to God,

00:42:27.439 --> 00:42:30.340
for her, it was a feast.

00:42:30.439 --> 00:42:33.340
It was a rich, rich time.

00:42:33.439 --> 00:42:36.340
For me, I was a beginner.

00:42:36.439 --> 00:42:39.340
And it was kind of a slog.

00:42:39.439 --> 00:42:40.340
Right?

00:42:40.439 --> 00:42:41.340
Can you kind of

00:42:41.439 --> 00:42:44.340
see the difference there?

00:42:44.439 --> 00:42:46.340
One way, well,

00:42:46.439 --> 00:42:47.340
and let me come back

00:42:47.439 --> 00:42:48.340
to that language of stress,

00:42:48.439 --> 00:42:49.340
hurry, worry, flurry.

00:42:49.439 --> 00:42:52.340
I do think certain

00:42:52.439 --> 00:42:54.340
cultural influences

00:42:54.439 --> 00:42:56.340
can kind of lend themselves

00:42:56.439 --> 00:42:58.340
to people of prayer

00:42:58.439 --> 00:43:01.340
or can kind of draw away.

00:43:01.439 --> 00:43:02.340
And you have,

00:43:02.439 --> 00:43:03.340
even to this day,

00:43:03.439 --> 00:43:04.340
certain kind of cultures

00:43:04.439 --> 00:43:05.340
that are so powerfully

00:43:05.439 --> 00:43:08.340
influenced by their religion

00:43:08.439 --> 00:43:09.340
that it's almost like

00:43:09.439 --> 00:43:10.340
kind of in the air

00:43:10.439 --> 00:43:11.340
and in the water,

00:43:11.439 --> 00:43:12.340
so to speak,

00:43:12.439 --> 00:43:14.340
of quiet and contemplation

00:43:14.439 --> 00:43:15.340
and, you know, I mean,

00:43:15.439 --> 00:43:16.340
I think, for example,

00:43:16.439 --> 00:43:18.340
of maybe like Tibetan culture

00:43:18.439 --> 00:43:20.340
with its Tibetan Buddhist influence.

00:43:20.439 --> 00:43:21.340
They're just kind of

00:43:21.439 --> 00:43:23.340
prayer kind of people.

00:43:23.439 --> 00:43:25.340
You know?

00:43:25.439 --> 00:43:26.340
Certain Indian influences,

00:43:26.439 --> 00:43:27.340
like it's just

00:43:27.439 --> 00:43:28.340
on the continent of India,

00:43:28.439 --> 00:43:29.340
like it's just,

00:43:29.439 --> 00:43:30.340
there's a certain culture.

00:43:30.439 --> 00:43:31.340
I do think in the West,

00:43:31.439 --> 00:43:32.340
although we have a powerful,

00:43:32.439 --> 00:43:33.340
strong kind of roots

00:43:33.439 --> 00:43:34.340
in Christian faith,

00:43:34.439 --> 00:43:36.340
mostly the culture,

00:43:36.439 --> 00:43:38.340
I don't think we're,

00:43:38.439 --> 00:43:39.340
I wouldn't consider us

00:43:39.439 --> 00:43:41.340
a super prayerful culture.

00:43:41.439 --> 00:43:42.340
You know?

00:43:42.439 --> 00:43:43.340
Quite the opposite.

00:43:43.340 --> 00:43:44.239
We are a culture.

00:43:44.340 --> 00:43:46.239
We're like the go people.

00:43:46.340 --> 00:43:47.239
You know what I mean?

00:43:47.340 --> 00:43:48.239
And even our religious practice,

00:43:48.340 --> 00:43:50.239
like what are we awesome at?

00:43:50.340 --> 00:43:51.239
Doing things.

00:43:51.340 --> 00:43:52.239
You know what I mean?

00:43:52.340 --> 00:43:53.239
Like you think of

00:43:53.340 --> 00:43:54.239
kind of Western Christianity

00:43:54.340 --> 00:43:55.239
